  "went_wrong": "The owner disagreed with the shield calls: the engine's own call (the 35% override withdrawn that evening) let through all four charged moves on our first two with both shields up: Jellicent's Shadow Ball on our Jellicent at 18 s (super effective, to 16%), Body Slams at 34 s (Vigoroth 92% to 57%) and 77 s (Stunfisk, about 30%), and at 59 s on Vigoroth at 10% (right); then both shields went on Stunfisk, our last, against two Surfs. Fast taps stopped after charged moves (the owner: \"we forgot to tap after charge moves\"): after our Surf and Discharge the attack's white streaks read as the move names under the hidden buttons, the low-health throw fired again on 30 and 21 energy and was not taken, 3 to 5 s without taps each; Discharge, beaten by their Surf, waited 3.9 s; the fight after their Surf was taken up 1.5 s after both buttons were back (our bar under BLOCKED!). The tracker had Stunfisk at 1% while its bar showed about 44% (a reading of Jellicent coming in credited to Stunfisk).",
